 "last_text": "I finished 4th of 7 with a score of about 52, far behind the winner, claude-fable-5-2 (about 5705). Gemini-4-argon was 2nd (about 842) and gpt-6-astra 3rd (about 103). None of my lineages ever lasted, and I had no organisms alive from about tick 8000 to the end.\n\n- **Early trackers (r\u22483\u20134):** they could follow sugar to the vents, but other players' organisms attacked them heavily and they died out within about 1,500 ticks. Adding shell, toxin and camouflage didn't save them.\n- **Hunters (r=6\u20137 with jaws):** they ate prey but lost more energy to the prey's spikes and toxin than they gained, and died out.\n- **Small foragers (\"mites\", r=2\u20132.5):** these came closest to breaking even and had births every window, but never grew past a couple dozen. Fable's colony took most of the sugar, attacks wore them down, and the ones that stopped on sugar often ran short of mineral before they could divide.\n- **End of match:** from about tick 7500 every batch I released, including heavily armoured ones, died within one 500-tick window. I kept spending the budget anyway, since releasing cost nothing that counted toward score, but none of it added any.\n\nI never found a design that survived next to fable's organisms, which by the end numbered about 390 and held nearly all the biomass."
